BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Sketching with Sami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261116T120000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb3a0@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join Sami as we sketch the local plants in Holbrook-Palme
 r Park. Together\, we can learn more about what is blooming locally\, so t
 hat when we take walks outside in the future\, we will be able to recogniz
 e what is growing alongside us. Some techniques that will be taught by Sam
 i include how to sketch flowers and how to mix watercolors so that they ap
 pear more natural."\n\nSpace is limited\, and registration is required. Re
 gistrants will be emailed the exact location in Holbrook-Palmer Park.\n\nA
 ges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRe
 gistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f
 6edd4fa0c68b5eb3a0\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb3a0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Atherton Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260826T120000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-696aab8eb0595799c096cda2@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the Atherton Book Club every fourth Wednesday of t
 he month from 11:00 AM - 12:00 PM. We will be engaging in fun and lively d
 iscussions about books each month. We want to create a safe environment wh
 ere everyone feels welcome and heard. All book club participants can nomin
 ate book selections\, and we vote on the selection as a group. Please join
  us!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for 
 them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/even
 ts/696aab8eb0595799c096cda2\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/696aab8eb0595799c096cda2
END:VEVENT
