UID:smcl-695848ade3e3999b5c057d47@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a fun and healthy way to connect with others? Join
  the \nAtherton Library's  Walking Club and explore the scenic beauty of H
 olbrook Palmer Park\n while enjoying the fresh air and good company. Walki
 ng regularly offers\n numerous health benefits\, including improved cardio
 vascular health\, \nstronger bones\, better balance\, enhanced mood\, and 
 increased energy \nlevels.\n\nThis group is a great way to stay active\, m
 eet new friends\, and \ndiscover the joy of walking together. Routes withi
 n the park are \naccessible and paced to accommodate all fitness levels. C
 omfortable \nshoes and a sense of adventure are all you need to participat
 e!\n\nSpecial Walks – Every Third Friday! \n\n\nWe’re excited to intro
 duce\nSpecial Walks on the third Friday of every month! These outings will
  take us to scenic locations just a 15-minute drive from\nthe Atherton Lib
 rary\, offering new trails and beautiful views.\n\n\n\nVisit our Walking C
 lub Hub for more information and updates!\n\n\nThe walking club will meet 
 at the Jennings Pavilion at Holbrook Palmer Park. Let’s step into wellne
 ss together!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not desig
 ned for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/
 events/695848ade3e3999b5c057d47\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/695848ade3e3999b5c057d47
END:VEVENT
