 olbrook Palmer Park\n while enjoying the fresh air and good company. Walki
 ng regularly offers\n numerous health benefits\, including improved cardio
 vascular health\, \nstronger bones\, better balance\, enhanced mood\, and 
 increased energy \nlevels.\n\nThis group is a great way to stay active\, m
 eet new friends\, and \ndiscover the joy of walking together. Routes withi
 n the park are \naccessible and paced to accommodate all fitness levels. C
 omfortable \nshoes and a sense of adventure are all you need to participat
 e!\n\nSpecial Walks – Every Third Friday! \n\n\nWe’re excited to intro
 duce\nSpecial Walks on the third Friday of every month! These outings will
  take us to scenic locations just a 15-minute drive from\nthe Atherton Lib
 rary\, offering new trails and beautiful views.\n\n\n\nVisit our Walking C
 lub Hub for more information and updates!\n\n\nThe walking club will meet 
 at the Jennings Pavilion at Holbrook Palmer Park. Let’s step into wellne
 ss together!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not desig
 ned for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/
 events/695848ade3e3999b5c057d39\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/695848ade3e3999b5c057d39
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Fall in Love With the Classics at Holbrook Palmer Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T113000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-6a02440a8e677a28001b57ab@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us this fall for a three-part classic literature discussi
 on series exploring love\, ambition\, and social expectations through unfo
 rgettable novels. We’ll meet monthly from August through November on the
  third Wednesday of the month for welcoming and engaging conversations. \n
 \n\nAt the first meeting\, we will introduce the structure of the series\,
  distribute the first book\, and give participants a chance to meet fellow
  readers before discussions begin.  Books will be provided. Attendance a
 t each discussion meeting is required in order to receive the next book in
  the series.\n\nOur first featured novel is Jane Austen’s Northanger Abb
 ey\, a witty and charming satire that follows young Catherine Morland as s
 he navigates friendship\, romance\, and imagination. Filled with humor and
  sharp social commentary\, Austen’s novel playfully examines the influen
 ce of gothic fiction and society’s expectations.\n\nThe book club will m
 eet at North Meadow Picnic Tables at Holbrook Palmer Park\n\nAges: Adult p
 rogram (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: 
 none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a02440a8e677a28001b57
 ab\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a02440a8e677a28001b57ab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Sketching with Sami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T120000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join Sami as we sketch the local plants in Holbrook-Palme
 r Park. Together\, we can learn more about what is blooming locally\, so t
 hat when we take walks outside in the future\, we will be able to recogniz
 e what is growing alongside us. Some techniques that will be taught by Sam
 i include how to sketch flowers and how to mix watercolors so that they ap
 pear more natural."\n\nSpace is limited\, and registration is required. Re
 gistrants will be emailed the exact location in Holbrook-Palmer Park.\n\nA
 ges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRe
 gistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f
 6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Meet James Wang\, Author of What You Need to Know About AI\,
  in Conversation with Justin Kuczynski
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T160000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-6a513ae1e9de6536001ac257@local-events
DESCRIPTION:San Mateo County Libraries welcomes James Wang\, author of WHA
 T YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT AI\, for a timely and engaging conversation with 
 featured host Justin Kuczynski.  \n\nArtificial intelligence is shaping th
 e way we work\, learn\, create and connect. Whether you are new to AI or a
 lready following the latest developments\, this author talk offers a clear
  and welcoming place to explore what AI is\, why it matters and how it may
  shape our shared future.  \n\nA book signing will follow the talk. Free c
 opies of What You Need to Know About AI will be available at the door\, wh
 ile supplies last. Giveaway copies are limited and offered on a first-come
 \, first-served basis. \n\nAbout the Book \n\nIn What You Need to Know Abo
 ut AI\, James Wang cuts through the noise around one of today’s most tal
 ked-about technologies. With clarity and insight\, he explores the history
 \, principles and real-world implications of AI\, helping readers better u
 nderstand a fast-changing field that is already influencing daily life.  \
 n\nMeet James Wang \n\nJames Wang is a technologist\, investor and writer 
 with over a decade of experience in AI and deep tech. He is a general part
 ner at Creative Ventures\, an early-stage deep tech fund backing breakthro
 ughs in AI\, synthetic biology and advanced materials.  \n\nPreviously\, J
 ames worked at Bridgewater Associates and worked at Google's "moonshot" in
 novation lab\, X. He has served as a board director at startups working in
  AI\, healthcare and robotics and is a regular guest lecturer at UC Berkel
 ey on entrepreneurship and startup financing.  \n\nMeet Featured Host Just
 in Kuczynski \n\nJustin Kuczynski is an engineering lead and technologist 
 with over a decade of experience in machine learning and computational sci
 ence. He currently works on large-scale systems at Google\, where he focus
 es on building the complex modeling infrastructure that powers modern digi
 tal tools.\n\nPreviously\, Justin earned a PhD in computational biology an
 d spent years working at the intersection of tech and the life sciences\, 
 building and applying machine learning models to solve fundamental challen
 ges in human health. Having tracked the evolution of data-driven modeling 
 from early academic research to industry applications\, he maintains high 
 hopes for AI's potential to improve human health and generally aid human f
 lourishing.\n\n\n\nJoin us for an inspiring afternoon of learning\, connec
 tion and exploration as James Wang and Justin Kuczynski help make the worl
 d of AI feel more approachable\, relevant and connected to our everyday li
 ves.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for 
 them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6
 a513ae1e9de6536001ac257\nLast synced: 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a513ae1e9de6536001ac257
END:VEVENT
