BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Watercolor Painting in the Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T120000
DTSTAMP:20260724T042407Z
UID:smcl-6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we will explore the historical buildings an
 d diversity of trees in Holbrook Palmer Park\, and learn to make field ske
 tches in watercolor\, identify a picture frame in the field\, and construc
 t a quick composition with focal point\, contrast\, light\, and shadow. So
 me experience with drawing and painting is helpful.\n\nWe will meet in the
  first parking lot of Holbrook-Palmer Park. Registration is required\, and
  space is limited. \n\nThe library will provide some basic supplies. If y
 ou do plan to bring your own\, here is what the instructor recommends:\nsk
 etchbook with watercolor paper\nwatercolor travel kit and brushes\na small
  portable water container\nfolding stool or camping chair\nRegistration wi
 ll open on Monday\, July 13 @ 10:00 am. Please note that you will need to
  register for each individual session.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcom
 e to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: h
 ttps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3\nLast synced
 : 2026-07-23 21:24 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3
